WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.370
- All right, so this
show always finishes up

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.590
with something cool
trending on social media.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.150
And today's no different, everybody.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.091
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:07.091 --> 00:00:10.650
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.010
All hour, we've celebrated
love, life, and relationships

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.160
with the cast of "The Best
Man: The Final Chapters."

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.710
Well, when you've dated
someone for more than a decade,

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.427
the question comes up a lot.

00:00:21.427 --> 00:00:23.280
"When are you gonna tie the knot?"

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.730
One South Carolina bride
wanted to make sure

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.570
she heard her friends and
family loud and clear.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.310
After 15 years with her man,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.013
this is how she started her
vows on her wedding day.

00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:41.967
(wedding attendees laughing)

00:00:49.425 --> 00:00:51.286
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:51.286 --> 00:00:52.711
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:52.711 --> 00:00:56.580
She's literally my favorite
human on planet Earth.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.690
You can see everybody loved
it in not only our audience,

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.820
but there at the wedding
as well. It was hilarious.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.640
And we have these newlyweds
on the line right now

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.220
watching on WYFF News 4.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.240
What's up, Christie? What's up, Byron?

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.520
(audience cheering)

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.720
- Hey, Kelly.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.870
- Hey. First of all, girl, you are funny.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.260
That was the funniest thing
I've ever seen at a wedding.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.440
And secondly, Byron,
congrats to both of you.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.750
Like, it looks like that
moment caught you off guard,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.002
and your face was hysterical, man.

00:01:27.002 --> 00:01:27.870
- Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.453
It did definitely catch me off guard.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.390
When she was handed her vows,

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:35.460
I looked down and I was like,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.920
these vows just don't look right.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:41.313
And then she blew the dust
and I was like, what is that?

00:01:42.286 --> 00:01:43.650
(Kelly and Christie laugh)
And it took me a second.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:47.280
I was like, okay, okay,
you got me on this one.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.760
But I think that that
culminated in a good moment

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.350
and a very special moment

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.600
and we're just happy
to be married for sure.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.800
(audience applauding)

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.300
- It's literally my favorite thing

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.100
I've ever seen at a wedding.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.620
So, Christie, you say it wasn't just about

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.720
being funny, though, right, in the moment?

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.450
- Right, I was very emotional
leading up to the wedding

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.210
so I knew that if I didn't
do something to break the ice

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:12.510
and kind of at least make myself chuckle,

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.510
that I was gonna cry throughout my vows.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.350
So when I did it

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.960
and everybody burst into
laughter, I was shocked.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.460
But it actually really worked.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.280
And after everybody calmed
down from the laughing,

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.750
I made my way through the vows

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.200
and everything that we've
been praying for and wanting

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.360
came to fruition and we were married,

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.190
and the day was perfect
and it was beautiful.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.530
We just kind of find
ourselves wanting to relive it

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.700
over and over again.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.070
- Oh my gosh. Well, thank y'all so much.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.350
Thank you Christie and Byron
for sharing that with us.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.240
I wish you a lifetime of happiness

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.440
and you've already had pretty much

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.990
a good life already
together, which is awesome.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.935
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:47.935 --> 00:02:48.870
(bell dings)

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:49.703
But that's not all,

00:02:49.703 --> 00:02:52.020
our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.330
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.460
want to celebrate your love

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.950
and how it stood the test of time already.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.496
So they're gonna give you
$1000, how's that sound?

00:03:01.496 --> 00:03:03.060
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.130
- Oh my gosh. Thank you so much.

00:03:07.098 --> 00:03:09.000
- Absolutely. All because of some dust.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.770
That was hilarious.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.150
Well, thank you guys so much.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.700
And by the way, in case
everybody out there,

